# Semgrep exclusions — code that is not CLARA's to review.
#
# The shipped application (api/, web/app/, web/assets/js/) is scanned in full and
# never listed here. Its findings are triaged per site in
# docs/Static_Analysis_Triage.md, deliberately without inline `nosemgrep`
# markers, so a real finding cannot hide behind a suppression comment.

# Historic FIONA user-management application — the example layout AGENTS.md
# ("Repository layout") points at when PHP needs to interface with the web
# application. It really does hash passwords with MD5, disable TLS peer
# verification and name request files after the submitted username: that is the
# state CLARA replaces. Rewriting it would misrepresent the reference, so it is
# out of scope rather than waived finding by finding.
assets/

# Vendored third-party libraries (Bootstrap, Tabulator, D3, Geist, Swagger UI),
# copied locally instead of loaded from a CDN per REQ-TECH-021. Upstream code;
# the fix for a finding in it is a newer upstream copy.
web/assets/vendor/
api/docs/swaggerui/

# Development and CI tooling, never deployed (REQ-TECH-028): Playwright runs and
# capture scripts, the load generator, test fixtures and helper scripts. They
# speak plain HTTP to a localhost server on purpose, build regular expressions
# out of their own arguments, and use the stdlib TLS/HTTP clients in ways the
# audit rules flag without a weakness behind them.
docs/
e2e/
stress/
tests/
tools/
ci/

# Minified bundles — machine output, including the copies under assets/.
**/*.min.js
**/*.min.css

# Go tests and the test-only database helper. Not deployed: `go build` leaves `_test.go` out of
# the binary, and internal/testdb is imported only by those tests (REQ-TECH-028's "test fixtures
# and helper scripts"). Their findings are fake secrets and throwaway DDL by construction — a
# bcrypt hash of a known test password, a fixed TOTP seed, a TLS server the test itself starts —
# so reviewing them would train nobody. The code under review is the same package's non-test files,
# which stay in scope.
**/*_test.go
api/internal/testdb/
